# NovaBank Management System

A console-based banking management system written in pure Java (no external libraries). It supports multiple account types, money transfers, an undo feature, real-time event alerts, monthly interest, and persistent storage.

## Why this design is different

Most student banking projects are a single class with a menu and a list of balances. NovaBank is built around a few ideas that make it closer to how real banking software works:

| Feature | What it does | Pattern / concept |
|---|---|---|
| Polymorphic accounts | Savings and Current accounts share one interface but have different rules (overdraft, interest) | Inheritance, abstract classes |
| Live event feed | Every account opening, large transfer, and interest run is broadcast to subscribers | Observer pattern |
| Fraud watch | Movements at or above a threshold trigger an alert | Event-driven rules |
| Undo last operation | Reverses the most recent deposit, withdrawal, or transfer | Stack-based compensation |
| Atomic transfers | If the credit side fails, the debit is rolled back automatically | Compensating transaction |
| Full statements | Every account keeps a timestamped ledger with running balances | Immutable records (Java `record`) |
| Exact money maths | All amounts use `BigDecimal`, never `double` | Correct financial arithmetic |
| Persistence | Accounts are saved to a CSV file and reloaded on startup | File I/O |

